"sentences": [
{
"scene": 1,
"text": "This boy would conquer most of the known world before his thirty-third birthday.",
"s": 0.25,
"e": 4.261
},
{
"scene": 1,
"text": "It's 356 BC, in the kingdom of Macedonia, and a prince named Alexander is born.",
"s": 4.401,
"e": 10.233
},
{
"scene": 2,
"text": "His father, King Philip the Second, is turning Macedonia into a military powerhouse.",
"s": 10.553,
"e": 15.662
},
{
"scene": 2,
"text": "As a boy, Alexander tames a wild horse nobody else can ride, just by turning it toward the sun, because it was scared of its own shadow.",
"s": 15.802,
"e": 24.029
},
{
"scene": 2,
"text": "So Philip hires the smartest man in Greece to teach him. Aristotle.",
"s": 24.169,
"e": 28.181
},
{
"scene": 2,
"text": "Philosophy, mathematics, medicine, and how to lead an army.",
"s": 28.321,
"e": 31.717
},
{
"scene": 3,
"text": "Then, in 336 BC, Philip is assassinated by one of his own bodyguards, at a wedding.",
"s": 32.037,
"e": 38.026
},
{
"scene": 3,
"text": "Suddenly, Alexander is king. He's twenty years old.",
"s": 38.166,
"e": 40.997
},
{
"scene": 4,
"text": "And he has a plan: invade the Persian Empire, the biggest superpower on Earth.",
"s": 41.317,
"e": 45.712
},
{
"scene": 4,
"text": "At Issus, he charges straight at the Persian king, Darius, who turns his chariot around and runs.",
"s": 45.852,
"e": 51.485
},
{
"scene": 4,
"text": "Two years later, at Gaugamela, Darius brings a much bigger army.",
"s": 51.625,
"e": 55.53
},
{
"scene": 4,
"text": "Alexander punches a hole right through the middle, and Darius runs away again.",
"s": 55.67,
"e": 59.637
},
{
"scene": 5,
"text": "Egypt welcomes him as a pharaoh. Persia falls.",
"s": 59.957,
"e": 62.764
},
{
"scene": 5,
"text": "He keeps marching, through Central Asia and all the way into India, until his exhausted army finally refuses to go any further.",
"s": 62.904,
"e": 70.825
},
{
"scene": 6,
"text": "Back in Egypt, in 331 BC, he had marked out a new city with barley flour, because the builders ran out of chalk.",
"s": 71.145,
"e": 78.759
},
{
"scene": 6,
"text": "Birds ate the whole plan. His priests called it a great sign, and they were right. Alexandria became one of the greatest cities on Earth.",
"s": 78.899,
"e": 86.785
},
{
"scene": 7,
"text": "Then, in 323 BC, in Babylon, Alexander catches a fever.",
"s": 87.105,
"e": 91.45
},
{
"scene": 7,
"text": "Days later, he's dead, at just thirty-two.",
"s": 91.59,
"e": 93.767
},
{
"scene": 8,
"text": "Asked who should rule his empire, he reportedly answered: the strongest.",
"s": 94.087,
"e": 97.989
},
{
"scene": 8,
"text": "So his generals fought over it, and it shattered into rival kingdoms.",
"s": 98.129,
"e": 101.823
},
{
"scene": 8,
"text": "But Greek language, art, and ideas now stretched from Egypt to India.",
"s": 101.963,
"e": 105.927
},
{
"scene": 8,
"text": "Nearly three hundred years later, Egypt's last queen still spoke Greek. Her name? Cleopatra.",
"s": 106.067,
"e": 111.468
},
{
"scene": 8,
"text": "All because one boy from Macedonia never lost a battle.",
"s": 111.608,
"e": 114.975
}
]
}